course: dictionary
lesson: 4067
title: Meet the geographer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A geographer is a person who studies geography. Geography is the study of the Earth: its land, seas, weather, places and the people who live there.
explain: The word gives a clue: a geographer is someone who studies the Earth. In geography lessons you work like a geographer, reading maps, measuring rivers and weather, and asking how places change.
explain: Read this: «Nobody in 1300 called it the Silk Road: a German geographer, Ferdinand von Richthofen, invented the name in 1877.» The clue is «invented the name». A geographer studies places, and this one gave a famous route its name.
fact: A geographer is a person who studies geography.
fact: Geography studies the Earth's land, seas, weather, places and people.
fact: «A famous geographer» is a geographer whose work is well known.
fact: Ferdinand von Richthofen was a German geographer.
fact: In 1877 he invented the name «Silk Road».
exercise: What is a geographer? | A person who fixes old clocks | A person who only studies numbers and sums | A person who paints pictures of animals | *A person who studies the Earth's land, seas, weather and people
exercise: In «a German geographer, Ferdinand von Richthofen, invented the name in 1877», what did he invent? | *The name «Silk Road» | A dinosaur | A new kind of ship
exercise: Which phrase means working the way a geographer does? | Read a comic and stop | *Work like a geographer, reading maps and measuring rivers | Work like a baker, making bread | Sleep until lunch
test: Which word means a person who studies the Earth? | Baker | Painter | *Geographer | Plumber
test: Which of these is studied in geography? | Ancient coins | Only the names of stars | *Rivers and the weather | Dance steps
exam: «A German geographer invented the name Silk Road in 1877.» Which word tells you what kind of person Richthofen was? | Chef | Musician | *Geographer | Pilot
